   "subject": "Colour picker input now available if anyone needs",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">If anyone wants to use a colour picker input, I implemented one in <a href=\"https://github.com/daattali/shinyjs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/daattali/shinyjs&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792398124640000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Dd3VniHWSM0vOp2Bdu_UP\">shinyjs</a>.  You can see a demo <a href=\"http://daattali.com/shiny/colourInput/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://daattali.com/shiny/colourInput/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792398124640000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2hqxKCMPRDLv2sunRPDBeN\">here</a><div><div><br></div><div>It&#39;s as easy to use as any other input: </div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"color:#000\">colourInput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;col&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;label&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;red&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>updateColourInput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;col&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> value </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;#123abc&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></font></div></code></div><br>It has a few other features such as supporting choosing the &quot;transparent&quot; colour</div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
