    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks Joe, I didn&#39;t know about those functions. Is that the preferred way that shiny inputs will be migrating to?<div>I didn&#39;t want to bother you until after useR, but since you already took a look at the code, I wanted to ask you if I can make a PR to shiny or do you not think that shiny core will take something like this?  I tried making the code as clean and robust as possible and mimic the other inputs as closely as possible, and added support for IE8+. The JavaScript library used is at <a href=\"https://github.com/daattali/jquery-colourpicker\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/daattali/jquery-colourpicker&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792398124654000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0EBbNXIl7J0Lyqe7ZaxnzI\">https://github.com/daattali/jquery-colourpicker</a> - it&#39;s a fork of a very popular repo (&gt;600 stars) with many modifications I made to make it geared to work with shiny.  Both the original author and myself are using MIT license.</div><div>Let me know if you think that&#39;d be possible</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br clear=\"all\"><div><div class=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>---</div><div><a href=\"http://deanattali.com\" style=\"font-size:12.8000001907349px\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://deanattali.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792398124654000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1fDb6oheOJJ2J-S0JZrI-0\">http://deanattali.com</a><br></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
